  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.1.12 - Typed dates are never silently replaced: HasInvalidInput reports an invalid entry kept under InvalidValueAction.Keep, CommitText() parses the box on demand, and an empty box means no date under Keep and SetToNull (behaviour change: Keep used to keep the old date). Persian and Arabic-Indic digits are accepted. New calendar-neutral SelectedDateTime (DateTime?, two-way). Auto mode follows a runtime culture switch via the static NotifyCultureChanged() / RefreshCalendar(), and switching CalendarType converts from the calendar the values are actually in. 2.0.0 - Breaking change: replaced Hour/Minute/Second properties on ModernPersianDatePicker (and Hour/Minute/Second on TimePickerView) with a single SelectedTime / Time property of type TimeSpan. Adds range-mode time support via RangeStartTime/RangeEndTime and a Quick Range panel that exposes time spinners on its From/To pickers.",
